<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Jan 4.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Jan 4.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to Jan 4 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>    Activity in week Dec 29-Jan 4</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,142,954 tns	117,799 tns    10.31 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,187,693 tns	108,329 tns     9.12 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,199,313 tns	119,943 tns    10.00 pct</p>
<p>    Total activity to Jan 4</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     5,706,257 tns	549,024 tns     9.62 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     4,888,448 tns	438,748 tns     8.98 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     5,396,660 tns	504,447 tns     9.35 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 47 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 51 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 51 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530. E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com))</p>
